    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0268" n="1002" xml:id="pg1002"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Butler to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Aug. 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 40.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation to my No. 38, of the 25th
                    instant, I have the honor to submit copies of additional papers in the matter of
                    the extradition of Chester W. and Richard Rowe.</p>
                <p>These papers include two notes from Mr. Mariscal—of the 22d (received on the
                    26th) and the 29th instants—declining to grant the extradition of Chester W.
                    Rowe, and reserving decision as to the extradition of Richard Rowe until the
                    arrival of the requisite papers.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. C. Butler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>








